Decision Annual_market_return
Title: Annual market return
Units: %/year
Description: Your estimates for the range of returns from the market for any given year. Low and High denote the 10% and 90% percentile estimates, and Mid is your median estimate -- the most typical percent return. A negative value means that the market loses value in a given year. The model assumes that the annual return has the same distribution for all years between now and your retirement, and that each year's return is statistically independent of the other years' returns. ~
~
From 1928 thru 2015, the 10-50-90 returns were -11%, 13.87% and 32.75%. The mean was 11.4%. You can adjust your estimates from these based on whether you think the average market returns have changed since then, whether your investment strategy will be more volatile or less volatile than the market as a whole, or whether you think the investments you are targeting behave differently.~
~
If you enter a formula that varies by time, then the distributions will vary with time, but will still be treated as statistically independent.
Definition: Table(LMH)(-0.11,0.1387,0.3275)
