Variable Unrealized_gain
Title: Unrealized gain
Units: $
Description: This is the amount of lingering gain (or profit) in investments since the time that they were purchased, at the beginning of the given time period. When you sell an investment, you realize the gain. For non-tax-advantaged accounts (i.e., a normal brokerage account), when you realize the gain you have to pay capital gains tax. For retirement accounts, the amount of unrealized gain doesn't really matter since realizing the gain isn't a tax event in those accounts.
Definition: Dynamic(0, ~
	Self[Time-1] - Sum( Capital_gain[Time-1], Gain_type) + Appreciation[Time-1] )
NodeLocation: 256,152,1
NodeSize: 64,24
WindState: 2,254,545,720,377
