Variable Capital_gain
Title: Capital gain
Units: $
Description: The profit (gain) on investments sold during this year -- i.e., the difference between the selling price and the purchase price of those investments.~
~
Unrealized gain tracks how much net profit (over purchase price) has accrued in your portfolio. To estimate your annual capital gains, this assumes that the ratio of this unrealized gain to your total investment value is reflected in the investments you sold this year. I.e., you were equally likely to sell investments that lost money as you were investments that have appreciated a lot, etc. This is an assumption that allows the model to estimate capital gains at a whole without having to track individual investments.
Definition: Amount_sold * Percent_unrealized
