Objective Realized_value_at_re
Title: Realized value at retirement
Units: $
Description: This is how much the retirement account is worth to you when you reach retirement. This isn't the same as the investment total at retirement, because you'll need to withdraw the money to actually use it, and various taxes will be due. This adjusts for both income taxes and capital gains taxes that will have to be paid when withdrawing the funds. Hence, this is a pretty reasonable objective measure of the value of the account to you.~
~
Because of many subtle complexities, this measure might not be a perfect measure of the true value to you. It does model the act of withdrawing your funds could actually change your tax bracket, and how that might impact the value of other income streams you have. Also, it doesn't attribute any value to future tax-free compounding in the account after your retirement begins.
Definition: (Investment_total_at_ -  Interm_profits_taxed * Capital_gains_tax_ra[Gain_type='Long-term'] * Unrealized_gains_at_)~
* (1 - Taxed_at_withdrawl_ * Retirement_tax_rate )
