Variable Tornado_for_Realize1
Title: Tornado for Realized Value at Retirement compared to 401k
Description: How sensitive is the net benefit of a plan, compared to a 401(k) plan, to changes in the various inputs? This result graph shows a convential tornado plot showing how the benefit compared to a 401(k) varies an each input is set to its low or high value, one at a time, with all other inputs kept at there base values.
Definition: if LMH='Med' then Mean(Effective_value_at_r)~
else ~
~
	(LocalAlias v := Tornado_inputs;~
	 For level := LMH do ~
		if level='Mid' then null else ~
			  WhatIf( Mean(Effective_value_at_r), v, Sensitivity_ranges[Tornado_inputs=Handle(v),LMH=level] )) ~

