Decision Current_tax_rate
Title: Current income tax rate
Units: %
Description: Your marginal tax bracket this year, when the funds are being placed into the investment account. This should include both state and local income tax rates.
Definition: 22%
NodeLocation: 112,312,1
NodeSize: 64,24
WindState: 2,437,497,720,350
Aliases: FormNode Fo1523387663
NumberFormat: 2,%,3,2,0,0,3,0,$,0,"ABBREV",0,,,0,0,15

Constant Taxed_up_front_
Title: Taxed up front?
Description: Specifies whether the money depositied in the account is pre-tax wages (not taxed up front) or post-tax wages (amount after income tax).
Definition: DetermTable(Account_type)(Checkbox(1),Checkbox(1),Checkbox(0),Checkbox(0))
NodeLocation: 112,240,1
NodeSize: 56,24
WindState: 2,556,497,720,350
DefnState: 2,922,194,416,303,,DFNM
{!40000|TableCellDefault: Checkbox(0)}

Variable Initial_investment_a
Title: Initial investment after pretax
Units: $
Description: The amount of funds that get deposited into your account this year after income taxes are applied.
Definition: Initial_investment * (1 - Taxed_up_front_ * Current_tax_rate) * (If Account_type='401k' and Employer401kMatching then 1+Employer_matching_pe else 1)
NodeLocation: 488,200,1
NodeSize: 64,32
WindState: 2,349,536,720,350
ValueState: 2,56,84,416,303,,MIDM

Decision Initial_investment
Title: Initial pre-tax investment
Units: $
Description: The amount invested this year in pre-tax dollars. In other words, the amount of your wages before this year's income tax is applied to those wages.~
~
In a traditional IRA or 401(k), all those pre-tax wages are invested. In a standard brokerage accound or Roth, income tax is deducted before investment.
Definition: $5000
NodeLocation: 112,48,1
NodeSize: 64,24
WindState: 2,477,545,720,350
Aliases: FormNode Fo1523387667

Variable Employer401kMatching
Title: Employer matches 401(k) contribution
Definition: Checkbox(0)
NodeLocation: 384,328,1
NodeSize: 64,32
Aliases: FormNode Fo1523466941
OnChange: ChangeNodeVisibility( Handle(Employer_matching_pe),~
	if SetContains(\Account_type,"401k") and Employer401kMatching then 'Visible' else 'Hidden',~
	what: 'UserInputs' )

Variable Employer_matching_pe
Title: Employer matching percent
Units: %
Description: A 100% matchi percent means that your employer matches your 401k contribution dollar-for-dollar. A 50% matching percent means the employer contributes $500 for every thousand dollars you contribute to the 401k. And so on.
Definition: 100%
