Text Benefit_sensitivity
Description: Realized value at retirement sensitivity
NodeLocation: 672,416,-1
NodeSize: 216,16
BalloonHelp: A sensitivity analysis panel. Use this to explore how sensitive the forecasts are to changes in the input assumptions.~
~
In the panel (table), you can directly edit the Low, Base and High estimates for each input. The base estimate are what you used to compute your model, and the Low, High values are used to compute the sensitivity ranges that appear as bars in the Resulting Increase/Decrease columns.~
~
The resulting decrease/increase columns show how much the Realized Value at Retirement would change if the corresponding input where changed to its low or high value, all other inputs kept at their base levels. This enables you to see which input factors have the most influence on your realized value at retirement.

Button Panel
